        "node_id": "n_1_a7f993",
        "thought_text": "Develop a greedy algorithm that processes boats in the order they arrive, raising the bridge immediately when a boat arrives and lowering it as soon as all waiting boats have passed. This approach ensures minimal bridge unavailability but may not always optimize for the 30-minute waiting limit.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794407187.855731
      },
      "rev_n_2_44f335_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_44f335_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_44f335",
        "thought_text": "Implement a dynamic programming solution where each state represents the optimal decision (raise or lower the bridge) given the current time and the number of boats that have arrived. This method would consider all possible scenarios to minimize bridge unavailability while adhering to the waiting limit.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794407187.855755
      },
      "rev_n_3_b96c5b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_b96c5b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_b96c5b",
        "thought_text": "Use a priority queue to manage boats based on their arrival times and the potential impact on subsequent boats' waiting times. This strategy would aim to balance the immediate needs of arriving boats with the future efficiency of bridge operations, ensuring no boat waits longer than 30 minutes.",
